From e4f213984db2bc9b21b6268b62bb24a3386e1038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FoundingEngineer <founding-engineer@privacywindow.app>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:46:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable PCIe BAR1 P2P on consumer Blackwell (RTX 5060 Ti /
 5090)

Port of aikitoria's 595.71.05 BAR1 P2P patch to 595.91.07.

Stock consumer drivers expose no working GPU-to-GPU P2P path: the mailbox
route is fused off and the BAR1 route is stubbed out on non-datacenter
parts. This routes peer mappings through BAR1 instead, which works on
consumer Blackwell once the BAR is resizable and large enough.

RM side:
  - kernel_bif.c: default p2pOverride to reads+writes (0x11) and select
    NV_REG_STR_RM_PCIEP2P_TYPE_BAR1 instead of the mailbox default.
  - kern_bus_gp100.c: dispatch _PCIE_BAR1 connection types to the
    BAR1 P2P create/remove HALs.
  - g_kern_bus_nvoc.c: point the five kbus*Bar1P2P* vtable slots at the
    GH100 implementations rather than the 395e98/d69453 stubs, which
    return "not supported" on consumer SKUs.
  - io_vaspace.c: drop the left-over-mapping assert in the IOVAS
    destructor; BAR1 P2P mappings legitimately outlive it.
  - nv_gpu_ops.c, osmemdesc.c: rewrite peer apertures to SYS_COH so the
    PTEs describe BAR1 as system-coherent memory.

Kernel side:
  - nv-reg.h: default NVreg_EnableResizableBar to 1. Without a resized
    BAR1 there is no window to map the peer through.
  - os-mlock.c, nv-dma.c, nv.c: carry the hugepage compound order
    alongside locked user pages, via a hidden header on the page array,
    so 2 MB compound pages are not walked as 4 KB pages.
  - uvm_gpu.h: treat GB100+ as coherent so UVM's P2P registration takes
    the same route as the SYS_COH aperture rewrite above; otherwise the
    ZONE_DEVICE peer DMA setup conflicts with the BAR1-as-sysmem PTEs.

Requires "Above 4G Decoding" and Resizable BAR enabled in firmware, and
iommu=pt (see GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT).

Tested on 4x RTX 5060 Ti (16 GB), Ubuntu 22.04, kernel 5.15.0-190/-191:
nvidia-smi topo -p2p rw reports OK for all 12 ordered pairs.

Based on the 595.71.05 patch by aikitoria.
